"ENSG00000172403","module":"turquoise","kme":0.0567879,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.500479,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"CUX2+","gene_id":"ENSG00000172403","module":"brown","kme":0.32876,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.923266,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Inhibitory","gene_id":"ENSG00000172403","module":"magenta","kme":0.185526,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.378268,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Vascular.niche","gene_id":"ENSG00000172403","module":"yellow","kme":0.435427,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.709384,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false},"mathys2019":{"dataset_label":"Mathys et al. 2019","gene_ids":["ENSG00000172403"],"dataset_symbols":["SYNPO2"],"explorer":"explorer.html?dataset=mathys2019#gene/SYNPO2","cell_types":[{"cell_type":"Ex","gene_symbol":"SYNPO2","gene_symbol_current":"SYNPO2","gene_id":"ENSG00000172403","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":true,"nucleus_direction":"lower in AD","nucleus_padj":8.53489e-06,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.13134,"nucleus_score":-4.77187,"pct_ad":0.465055,"pct_control":0.501834,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.985617,"donor_log2fc":-0.104486,"donor_lfcse":0.0829891,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-1.57267e-05},{"cell_type":"In","gene_symbol":"SYNPO2","gene_symbol_current":"SYNPO2","gene_id":"ENSG00000172403","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":false,"nucleus_direction":"lower in AD","nucleus_padj":0.665456,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.188503,"nucleus_score":-1.07184,"pct_ad":0.137533,"pct_control":0.145658,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.999889,"donor_log2fc":-0.109978,"donor_lfcse":0.136982,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-6.21791e-06}],"modules":[{"cell_type":"In","gene_id":"ENSG00000172403","module":"red","kme":0.174033,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.737188,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000172403","entrez_id":["171024"],"uniprot":["Q9UMS6"],"ncbi_summary":"Enables alpha-actinin binding activity and filamin binding activity. Involved in positive regulation of actin filament bundle assembly; positive regulation of cell migration; and regulation of Rho-dependent protein serine/threonine kinase activity. Located in several cellular components, including Z disc; focal adhesion; and stress fiber. [provided by Alliance of Genome Resources, Apr 2022]","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q9UMS6","text":"Has an actin-binding and actin-bundling activity. Can induce the formation of F-actin networks in an isoform-specific manner (PubMed:23225103, PubMed:24005909). At the sarcomeric Z lines is proposed to act as adapter protein that links nascent myofibers to the sarcolemma via ZYX and may play a role in early assembly and stabilization of the Z lines. Involved in autophagosome formation. May play a role in chaperone-assisted selective autophagy (CASA) involved in Z lines maintenance in striated muscle under mechanical tension; may link the client-processing CASA chaperone machinery to a membrane-tethering and fusion complex providing autophagosome membranes (By similarity). Involved in regulation of cell migration (PubMed:22915763, PubMed:25883213). May be a tumor suppressor (PubMed:16885336). [Isoform 1]: Involved in regulation of cell migration. Can induce formation of thick, irregular actin bundles in the cell body. [Isoform 2]: Involved in regulation of cell migration. Can induce long, well-organized actin bundles frequently orientated in parallel along the long axis of the cell showing characteristics of contractile ventral stress fibers. [Isoform 3]: Involved in regulation of cell migration. Can induce an amorphous actin meshwork throughout the cell body containing a mixture of long and short, randomly organized thick and thin actin bundles. [Isoform 4]: Can induce long, well-organized actin bundles frequently orientated in parallel along the long axis of the cell showing characteristics of contractile ventral stress fibers. [Isoform 5]: Involved in regulation of cell migration in part dependent on the Rho-ROCK cascade; can promote formation of nascent focal adhesions, actin bundles at the leading cell edge and lamellipodia (PubMed:22915763, PubMed:25883213). Can induce formation of thick, irregular actin bundles in the cell body; the induced actin network is associated with enhanced cell migration in vitro."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}